    "text": "To determine how many servings of peanut butter Toby should add to his toast to reach a total of 500 calories, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the number of calories in one piece of bread.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Calories in one piece of bread} = 100\n   \\]\n\n2. Determine the total number of calories Toby wants to consume.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total calories desired} = 500\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate the number of calories from the peanut butter needed to reach the total of 500 calories.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Calories from peanut butter} = 500 - 100 = 400\n   \\]\n\n4. Determine how many servings of peanut butter are needed to provide 400 calories.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Servings of peanut butter} = \\frac{400}{200} = 2\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, Toby should add \\(\\boxed{2}\\) servings of peanut butter to his toast.",
